<p class="style2">AHARI</p>
<table align="center" bgcolor="#FFCCFF" width="90%">
<tr align="center"><td width="155" align="left" valign="middle">Raga  
<td width="607" align="left" valign="middle">AHARI</td>
</tr>
<tr align="center"><td align="left" valign="middle">Arohana	<td align="left" valign="middle">Sa Ri Sa Ma Ga Pa Dha Ni Sa</td></tr>
<tr align="center"><td align="left" valign="middle">Avarohana<td align="left" valign="middle">Sa Ni Dha Pa Ma Ga Ri Sa</td></tr>
<tr align="center"><td align="left" valign="middle">Other Names
<td align="left" valign="middle">Aahiri</td>
</tr>
<tr align="center"><td align="left" valign="middle">Janya of	<td align="left" valign="middle">Vakulabharana or Hanumathodi</td></tr>
<tr align="center"><td align="left" valign="middle">Applicable to<td align="left" valign="middle">Shoka. </td></tr>
<tr align="center"><td align="left" valign="top">Examples
<td align="left" valign="middle"><p>1. Nalacharitham 1 "Kandalethrayum Kauthukam" was in Ahari. Now changed to Erikila Kamodari.
<br>
2. Narakasura Vadham."Sudhashanendra Vada" </p>
  </td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="style2">ANANDA BHAIRAVI </p>
<table align="center" bgcolor="#FFCCFF" width="90%">
  <tr align="center">
    <td width="155" align="left" valign="middle">Raga  
    <td width="607" align="left" valign="middle">ANANDA BHAIRAVI </td>
  </tr>
  <tr align="center">
    <td align="left" valign="middle">Arohana	
    <td align="left" valign="middle">Sa Ga Ri Ga Ma Pa Dha Pa Sa</td>
  </tr>
  <tr align="center">
    <td align="left" valign="middle">Avarohana
    <td align="left" valign="middle">Sa Ni Dha Pa Ma Ga Ri Sa</td>
  </tr>
  <tr align="center">
    <td align="left" valign="middle">Other Names
    <td align="left" valign="middle">Nil</td>
  </tr>
  <tr align="center">
    <td align="left" valign="middle">Janya of	
    <td align="left" valign="middle">Nabhairavi or Kharaharapriya</td>
  </tr>
  <tr align="center">
    <td align="left" valign="middle">Applicable to
    <td align="left" valign="middle">Shoka or Karuna in Kathakali ( Unlike the name suggests)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr align="center">
    <td align="left" valign="top">Examples
    <td align="left" valign="middle"><p>1. Kuchela Patni to Kuchela &quot;Sarasa Nethra Porume&quot;<br>
2. Kalakeya Vadham &quot;Daivame , ha ha Daivame&quot; <br>
3. Rambha in Ravana Vijayam &quot;Ashara Nadha Munjama&quot;<br>
4. Gopalas in Uttara Swayamvara &quot;Paahi Mam, Veera , Paahi Mam&quot;</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
